==Stadium and sponsors==

===Stadium===
[[File:OmaSp Stadion 17.6.2017.jpg|260px|thumb|[[OmaSP Stadion]]]]
{{main|OmaSP Stadion}}
SJK play their home matches at [[OmaSP Stadion]]. Previously SJK played their home matches at [[Seinäjoen keskuskenttä]].

In 2010, it was reported for the first time that SJK were planning a [[OmaSP Stadion|new football stadium]]. Eventually, in autumn 2014 it was announced that the construction of SJK's [[OmaSP Stadion|new stadium]] would start soon. The construction began in summer 2015 and the new stadium was completed in June 2016.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://stadiumdb.com/designs/fin/seinajoki_stadion|title=Design: Seinäjoki Stadion – StadiumDB.com|work=stadiumdb.com|access-date=9 March 2017|archive-date=21 June 2016|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160621054946/http://stadiumdb.com/designs/fin/seinajoki_stadion|url-status=live}}</ref> Stadium has a capacity of 5817 seats.

SJK play their friendlies and cup matches during the winter at [[Wallsport Areena]] which is an indoor training facility owned and operated by the team.

